{
  "dom_id": "step-587434",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying a Trajectory Given a Starting Point and the Vector Field",
  "problem": "A sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown below (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Sketch the trajectory of the solution starting at the marked point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14118584/assets/0cf7942e618f0465ead5b98c6404a3747e505db75517725971c833c97121ab64.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, moving along with the flow (downward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14118584/assets/105bdbdcac5f0ff20f71a0131bf5bb3cbafe0e93ce8bc733a51c2dcb3fb8364f.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues downward, but the trajectory starts to turn slightly to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14118584/assets/96757a3aee3b161b2ba9887cd85f977f063807779604647dd791cf265790cabc.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues to go downwards and slightly to the left to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14118584/assets/658c15d2291368d0e6836ba19b90157d49dee4a510d58cddf7f85ddc9ff72a8d.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-587434\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"587434\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"21588\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-587434\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-10\">Identifying a Trajectory Given a Starting Point and the Vector Field</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"587434\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <p>A sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown below (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Sketch the trajectory of the solution starting at the marked point.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-d259112c09bd560643afeb7ef35f3134\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/d259112c09bd560643afeb7ef35f3134\"></div>\n            </div>     \n\n            <div class=\"explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n\n            <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>Let's sketch the trajectory.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>We start at the given point, moving along with the flow (downward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.33ex\" height=\"1.676ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -576.1 572.5 721.6\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">x</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E1-MJMATHI-78\" d=\"M52 289Q59 331 106 386T222 442Q257 442 286 424T329 379Q371 442 430 442Q467 442 494 420T522 361Q522 332 508 314T481 292T458 288Q439 288 427 299T415 328Q415 374 465 391Q454 404 425 404Q412 404 406 402Q368 386 350 336Q290 115 290 78Q290 50 306 38T341 26Q378 26 414 59T463 140Q466 150 469 151T485 153H489Q504 153 504 145Q504 144 502 134Q486 77 440 33T333 -11Q263 -11 227 52Q186 -10 133 -10H127Q78 -10 57 16T35 71Q35 103 54 123T99 143Q142 143 142 101Q142 81 130 66T107 46T94 41L91 40Q91 39 97 36T113 29T132 26Q168 26 194 71Q203 87 217 139T245 247T261 313Q266 340 266 352Q266 380 251 392T217 404Q177 404 142 372T93 290Q91 281 88 280T72 278H58Q52 284 52 289Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMATHI-78\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span>-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-1e72cfbafb65f970d697dda4103fc713\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/1e72cfbafb65f970d697dda4103fc713\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Next, the flow continues downward, but the trajectory starts to turn slightly to the left. </li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-77ad3d8eb22bdba17fcf14e48052927e\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/77ad3d8eb22bdba17fcf14e48052927e\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>After that, the trajectory continues to go downwards and slightly to the left to infinity.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-a442afec461d42b693fbda69339f3689\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/a442afec461d42b693fbda69339f3689\"></div>\n            </div>           \n        </div>",
